================================================================================

 PURPOSE
 This is the editable MASTER of the public Genetics Quest game. Keep it in a
 PRIVATE repository. Do not upload this annotated master to GitHub Pages or a
 public repository; publish a separately prepared distribution build instead.

 WHAT IS IN THIS FILE
 - HTML: registration, five lessons, gameplay, scoring and public leaderboard.
 - CSS: layout, mobile-friendly styling, DNA and swirling orbital dots.
 - JavaScript: game question data, Punnett square interactions, score tracking,
   opt-in preferences and optional Google Sheets communication.
 - Instructor-only comment near the bottom: Google Apps Script backend example.

 WHAT TO CUSTOMIZE
 1. LOOK AND FEEL: edit the CSS in <style> near the top. Search for "orbit-"
    to change the swirling dot animation around the DNA circle.
 2. GAME TITLE AND INTRO: search for "GENETICS QUEST" or "YOUR GENES".
 3. LESSON TEXT: search for "MISSION_LESSONS" and edit the lesson HTML strings.
 4. QUESTIONS / ANSWERS: search for "QUESTIONS". Preserve each question's data
    shape, correct answer index and explanation when changing the quiz.
 5. MAXIMUM SCORE: 100 points per question before penalties; score calculations
    live near function check(). Update the backend's score cap if this changes.
 6. STUDENT CHECK-IN: search for "firstName", "lastName", "emailOptIn" and
    "leaderboardOptIn". Email is optional; email and leaderboard permissions
    must remain separate and unchecked by default.
 7. SCORE COLLECTION: set SCORE_ENDPOINT to a deployed Google Apps Script URL.
    An empty value means standalone practice mode; visitors' scores cannot be
    centrally collected until a backend is connected.
 8. LEADERBOARD: search for "loadLeaderboard" and "doGet" below.

 PRIVACY & SECURITY NOTES
 - Never paste passwords, API secrets, or private spreadsheet credentials into
   this HTML: all files delivered to browsers can be viewed by visitors.
 - Merely keeping THIS master private does NOT hide the JavaScript of any public
   build. Minification/obfuscation discourages copying but does not prevent it.
 - The example Apps Script accepts unverified browser-submitted scores, so it
   is suitable for informal practice, NOT tamper-proof grading.
 - Keep the Google results Sheet private, display only opted-in abbreviated
   names publicly, and maintain a genuine email unsubscribe workflow before
   sending promotional emails.
 - Avoid publishing learner personally identifiable information in Git commits.

 RECOMMENDED GITHUB SETUP
 Private repository: genetics-quest-source
   genetics_quest_MASTER_ANNOTATED.html  <-- this file
 Public website repository:
   genetics_quest.html                   <-- distribution build only

 BEFORE RELEASING A NEW VERSION
 [ ] Save a versioned private backup and test the game on phone + desktop.
 [ ] Verify all 25 questions, Punnett squares, lessons and results screen.
 [ ] Check required first/last name and optional email consent behavior.
 [ ] Ensure leaderboard opt-in is off by default; test opting out.
 [ ] Confirm backend URLs / public disclosures are intentional.
 [ ] Generate a separate minified/obfuscated public HTML from this master.
 [ ] Check that the public distribution excludes instructor-only comments.
================================================================================
